# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=..., set by the tsan test preset). Every entry needs a
# justification. Prefer fixing the code; TSan runs nightly and is advisory (docs/testing.md).
#
# libarrow and libparquet (conda-forge) are not built with TSan: the synchronization inside Arrow's thread pools and
# futures (e.g. the I/O pool that pre-buffers Parquet column chunks) is invisible to TSan, so a buffer that an Arrow
# I/O thread frees after the reader is done is reported as racing with the reader's earlier memcpy (first seen in the
# nightly of 2026-09-26: BaseMemoryPoolImpl<SystemAllocator>::Free vs snappy decompression). Suppress race reports
# whose stacks run through these libraries. Deliberately `race:` and not `called_from_lib:`: ignoring the libraries'
# interceptors hides their mutex locks, and an unlock that Arrow's inlined future callbacks then perform in another
# library is reported as "unlock of an unlocked mutex". Races confined to our own code are still reported.
race:libarrow.so
race:libparquet.so
